The Economic and Community Development Committee:

1. Requested the appropriate City staff to report back to the Economic and Community Development Committee at the July 14, 2026, Committee meeting on consumer protection issues related to ticket price “gouging” sporting and entertainment events as well as hidden fees for booking accommodations:

a. If these practices are occurring within the City of Toronto;

b. Any existing municipal authorities, policies, or enforcement tools related to these matters;

c. The nature and extent of consumer complaints or impacts;

d. Potential options for municipal action, advocacy, or intergovernmental coordination; and

e. Provincial policies, by-laws, or regulatory authorities in place related to ticket price gouging and hotel hidden fees added to advertised prices.

City Council on May 20 and 21, 2026, adopted the following:

1. City Council authorize the General Manager, Parks and Recreation, to approve the following eligibility criteria to reimburse the cost of insurance to permit a park oven:

a. non-profit organizations, charities, and community groups that have been involved in the establishment and ongoing operation of a park oven;

b. operate the ovens for multiple public events during one or more seasons;

c. provide opportunities for community education on oven use during public events;

d. submit proof of payment for insurance; and

e. submit a short report about the public events involving the oven.

2. City Council authorize the General Manager, Parks and Recreation to implement, on an annual basis, a process to allocate a maximum of $10,000 to reimburse the costs of insurance to permit a park oven, in accordance with criteria set out in Part 1 above and on terms acceptable to the General Manager, Parks and Recreation, starting with the following organizations in 2026:

a. Centre for Local Research into Public Space (Dufferin Grove Park, Ward 9);

b. Friends of Christie Pits (Christie Pits Park, Ward 11);

c. Fred Victor as Trustee for Friends of Regent Park (Regent Park, Ward 13);

d. Friends of Sorauren Park (Sorauren Park, Ward 4);

e. Neighbours of Dentonia Park (Dentonia Park, Ward 19);

f. Thorncliffe Park Women's Committee (R.V. Burgess, Ward 15); and

g. Second Rise (Alexandra Park, Ward 10).

